<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<QuickAction xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!-- THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT - a comment placed ABOVE
         <QuickAction> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
         matching parent xml file" error. It is also why there is no <description>: no quick
         action in this repo carries one (0 of 80 measured), QuickAction.Description is capped at
         255 characters, and a comment is repo-only and never sent to the Metadata API.

         ADDED 2026-08-26. User decision: "we don't need a quick action named 'Advance Stage';
         instead we need the NEXT STAGE NAME." One headless action PER DISPOSITION HOP, labelled
         with the stage the click lands on, replacing the single generic Advance Stage button on
         the DISPOSITION side of LOI__c. Same shape as Disposition__c.Advance_to_* (2026-08-19).

         🔴 THE LABEL IS THE ONLY THING THAT DIFFERS BETWEEN THESE ACTIONS. All three point at the
         SAME c/advanceRecordStage bundle as LOI__c.Advance_Stage, and that component names no
         object and holds no stage map: RecordStageAdvanceService derives the target from the
         record's CURRENT stage via CONFIG_BY_TYPE, keyed per RECORD TYPE. advance() takes only a
         recordId - the client could not send a target if it wanted to. So the label is a promise
         the page's visibility rule keeps, and the two must be kept in step BY HAND.

         THIS ONE: LOI_DISPOSITION_NEXT_STAGE maps 'Received' => 'Under Review', so
         LOI_Record_Page gates it on {!Record.Stage__c} EQUAL 'Received'. 'Received' is the only
         stage on Disposition_LOI that Acquisition_LOI does NOT also carry; the record-type
         criterion is still present for uniformity with the other two, which genuinely need it.

         ACQUISITION IS UNTOUCHED. LOI__c.Advance_Stage still serves Acquisition_LOI (Draft ->
         Under Review -> Submitted -> Negotiation -> Signed) and is not deleted, renamed or
         re-pointed; so do Mark_Countered and Mark_Completed at the 'Submitted' branch. -->
    <actionSubtype>Action</actionSubtype>
    <label>Under Review</label>
    <lightningWebComponent>advanceRecordStage</lightningWebComponent>
    <optionsCreateFeedItem>false</optionsCreateFeedItem>
    <type>LightningWebComponent</type>
</QuickAction>
